<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! sense.holder.reads ~ who holds the store, who spawned them, and whether the socket answers

`lares sense holders` reads every holder of the sensorium's store beside its spawner, and whether this vessel's own daemon socket answers (the end of the capture route). A leading sensorium name (`lares sense <sensorium> <verb>`) addresses any named sensorium; bare, the verb reads `memory`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ holders

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`holders` params=`~ the topology`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ sensorium-root

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`sensorium-root` params=`takes/host-path ~ the sensorium's root; the leading sensorium name threads it, absent the memory sensorium`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ local

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`local` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ reads this host's process table; this handler checks no ocap`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ read

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`read` params=`exit/0 fields/[[daemonOpen]] ~ the topology and the socket`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins`>>

!! skins ~ cli

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins/cli`>>

!!! lares sense holders

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`skin` name=`cli` params=`handler/host spells/[[lares sense holders]] ~ the terminal`>>
```

